{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls","id":1533593,"title":"Infectious werewolf bites / werewolf version of ghouls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-05T02:56:44-07:00","id":1533593,"title":"Infectious werewolf bites / werewolf version of ghouls","content":"So I came upon a werewolf antagonist book for vampires on drivethroughrpg and got me thinking.<br /> What about some power for werewolves to turn humans into discount werewolves like vampires do with ghouls?<br /> BSD have fomori that fit the bill somewhat, but they are more or less independent from werewolves and more of a generic Wyrm monster, ugly and unreliable.<br /> <br /> I was thinking about something like a gift that would make werewolf bites infectious for a human that would turn it into something like a &quot;wolf fomor&quot; but without inherent wyrm corruption. Visually something like Supernatural (tv series) werewolves. So basically immunity to delirium, transformation/human form power, natural weapons and physical boost powers, maybe more powers for more powerful ones from Fomori power list. To balance it out, can use drawbacks like getting aggravated from silver, full moon madness, increased hunger, etc. Would work only on moratal humans and impose ghoul like devotion to the one that turned them.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Would it work for WoD werewolves? Maybe only BSD?<br /> Also how would you go about structuring the gift? I was thinking around Rank 4, rage roll vs stamina.<br /> <br /> there is existing gift that turns humans into wolves, which is R5. So maybe make this one structured like R4 metis Rattler's Bite but with 'werewolf' venom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 04-05-2024, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T05:16:21-07:00","id":1533597,"title":"","content":"We have a werewolf version of ghouls, the kinfolk. Kinfolk can have gnosis, be mages, etc.<br /> <br /> If you want a more supernatural version, you could borrow the wolf-blooded from 2nd edition of Werewolf the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> But if it is the devotion part you seek, I don't think that fits any Gaian werewolf. The compelling of the vampires is unnatural and werewolves are all about nature. We already did away with Animal Attraction for its compelling effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T06:12:22-07:00","id":1533599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533597#post1533597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have a werewolf version of ghouls, the kinfolk. Kinfolk can have gnosis, be mages, etc.<br /> <br /> If you want a more supernatural version, you could borrow the wolf-blooded from 2nd edition of Werewolf the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> But if it is the devotion part you seek, I don't think that fits any Gaian werewolf. The compelling of the vampires is unnatural and werewolves are all about nature. We already did away with Animal Attraction for its compelling effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinfolk are fine, but they really come off more as discount witches with their gnosis + folk magic. Of course if they awaken, they are just Mages.<br /> I am not familiar with 2nd edition forsaken (different line for a note) wolf-blooded. Will check - thanks.<br /> Er... werewolves don't have much direct mind control, but they still have it (like &quot;Geas&quot; or &quot;obedience&quot;, or quite a lot of fear based compelling) and &quot;we did away&quot; with old version of Animal Attraction because of changing IRL political fashion. I only have W20 and it's still on page 278. There is enough 'mind control' in nature, usually parasites and insects.<br /> <br /> Interesting reaction tho. Anything you didn't like can already be accomplished by a BSD by making some fomori and conditioning them with few low level gifts and training. They already do.<br /> The difference that I offered was to make it cleaner, more streamlined and usable for other tribes besides BSD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 04-05-2024, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T06:46:41-07:00","id":1533600,"title":"","content":"Hm, I have to agree this wouldn't fit well with Gaian tribes, but I could see it as something of BSD/Wyrm origin that by itself is not inherently wyrmish. Some kind of bio-agent escaping from a Pentex lab that causes people to uncontrollably go quasi-Glabro and auto frenzy wouldn't be too outlandish as a plot device that mimics more classical werewolves. Maybe it only affects Kinfolk who have the disposition for it, they already have most of the other attributes you are looking for. As a side note, Kinfolk have an aptitude for hedge magic, and Shapeshifting is a Sorcery Path.<br /> <br /> The problem I see with making it a Gift effect is that if there were an easy way of passing on (half-)werewolf powers, it would be a thing. The Garou would definitely make use of the additional numbers they could gain from elevating Kinfolk into half-werewolves. The BSDs even more so, Hives are notorious for trying to outbreed the competition. Meaning it would affect the setting in a non-trivial way, if that is a concern to you.<br /> Conversely, if it is something outside of the control of the Garou, it presents them with the problem on how to deal with the situation. If you have Kinfolk suddenly half-changing (without wyrm taint), it challenges some fundamental traditions and customs of the tribes. The Mockery Breeds occupy a somewhat similar niche. If I were to introduce something like that, this would be my preferred route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T07:08:04-07:00","id":1533603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533600#post1533600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I have to agree this wouldn't fit well with Gaian tribes, but I could see it as something of BSD/Wyrm origin that by itself is not inherently wyrmish. Some kind of bio-agent escaping from a Pentex lab that causes people to uncontrollably go quasi-Glabro and auto frenzy wouldn't be too outlandish as a plot device that mimics more classical werewolves. Maybe it only affects Kinfolk who have the disposition for it, they already have most of the other attributes you are looking for. As a side note, Kinfolk have an aptitude for hedge magic, and Shapeshifting is a Sorcery Path.<br /> <br /> The problem I see with making it a Gift effect is that if there were an easy way of passing on (half-)werewolf powers, it would be a thing. The Garou would definitely make use of the additional numbers they could gain from elevating Kinfolk into half-werewolves. The BSDs even more so, Hives are notorious for trying to outbreed the competition. Meaning it would affect the setting in a non-trivial way, if that is a concern to you.<br /> <br /> Conversely, if it is something outside of the control of the Garou, it presents them with the problem on how to deal with the situation. If you have Kinfolk suddenly half-changing (without wyrm taint), it challenges some fundamental traditions and customs of the tribes. The Mockery Breeds occupy a somewhat similar niche. If I were to introduce something like that, this would be my preferred route.</div> </div> </div> </div>interesting take.<br /> As I said, it was finding a short werewolf book that reworked werewolves as more classical horror monsters for non-crossover vampire games that served as inspiration for the idea.<br /> Way I saw it - it's a way to get not insane and disgusting fomori rather then anything else. You would basically build a wolf themed fomor. You can already do it easily enough with some wolf/dog spirits and roleplaying if you have time. <br /> Can't really say it would be a game breaker, if Garou really wanted (could get their shit together) there are number of ways to increase their power. they just aren't orderly enough for it.<br /> <br /> But to limit the number, could tie it in to a gnosis or rage levels. Let's say make it either cost a permanent point or just make impossible to turn more then permanent gnosis/rage points of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T07:09:28-07:00","id":1533604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533599#post1533599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er... werewolves don't have much direct mind control, but they still have it (like &quot;Geas&quot; or &quot;obedience&quot;, or quite a lot of fear based compelling) and &quot;we did away&quot; with old version of Animal Attraction because of changing IRL political fashion. I only have W20 and it's still on page 278. There is enough 'mind control' in nature, usually parasites and insects.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that the garou aren't the types to have servants like vampires are nor have the same needs. Garou are limited not by daylight or blood hunger, but by their Rage. So they need those who don't have Rage to help them handle situations among humans that don't require combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533599#post1533599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting reaction tho. Anything you didn't like can already be accomplished by a BSD by making some fomori and conditioning them with few low level gifts and training. They already do.<br /> The difference that I offered was to make it cleaner, more streamlined and usable for other tribes besides BSD.</div> </div> </div> </div>The BSDs are a league of their own with their actions and deeds, they can't be grouped with the Gaian tribes. While Shadow Lords torture and Red Talons eat humans, neither do anything close to what the BSDs do. So while BSDs create fomori and condition them, that's unique to them. Gaian garou do not intentionally create kami or gorgons, let alone train them.<br /> <br /> There is a similar concept to what you are suggesting, though, among the creatures of the Wyrm; <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/War_Wolves\" target=\"_blank\">Warwolves.</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T07:12:12-07:00","id":1533605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533603#post1533603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> interesting take.<br /> As I said, it was finding a short werewolf book that reworked werewolves as more classical horror monsters for non-crossover vampire games that served as inspiration for the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use those, then? Garou don't have to have anything to do with these cursed/infected werewolves. In fact, it would give the setting a lot more interest if there truly were actual horror monsters werewolves alongside the spirit warrior ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T07:17:53-07:00","id":1533606,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this would be interesting to add, it would work for the Garou to get some shock troops, but I think that mechanically it's not that interesting, it would just be an extra resource for the player. Compared to Ghouls, that are tied to their masters, with exceptions, and need maintenance, in the case of a werewolf bite, even if they were trapped by the Garou nation, they would be free most of the time without the need for maintenance and they really wouldn't be of much help outside as shock troops since a Garou does everything they do and better, a vampire too, but in their case they have the disadvantage of not going out in daylight so the ghouls become useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T07:37:09-07:00","id":1533607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533606#post1533606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this would be interesting to add, it would work for the Garou to get some shock troops, but I think that mechanically it's not that interesting, it would just be an extra resource for the player. Compared to Ghouls, that are tied to their masters, with exceptions, and need maintenance, in the case of a werewolf bite, even if they were trapped by the Garou nation, they would be free most of the time without the need for maintenance and they really wouldn't be of much help outside as shock troops since a Garou does everything they do and better, a vampire too, but in their case they have the disadvantage of not going out in daylight so the ghouls become useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, kinfolk are regular humans+ because there is no need for ghoul-like servants.<br /> <br /> Plus, vampires have servants in classical horror, werewolves do not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T07:41:16-07:00","id":1533608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533604#post1533604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that the garou aren't the types to have servants like vampires are nor have the same needs. Garou are limited not by daylight or blood hunger, but by their Rage. So they need those who don't have Rage to help them handle situations among humans that don't require combat.<br /> <br /> The BSDs are a league of their own with their actions and deeds, they can't be grouped with the Gaian tribes. While Shadow Lords torture and Red Talons eat humans, neither do anything close to what the BSDs do. So while BSDs create fomori and condition them, that's unique to them. Gaian garou do not intentionally create kami or gorgons, let alone train them.<br /> <br /> There is a similar concept to what you are suggesting, though, among the creatures of the Wyrm; <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/War_Wolves\" target=\"_blank\">Warwolves.</a><br /> <br /> Use those, then? Garou don't have to have anything to do with these cursed/infected werewolves. In fact, it would give the setting a lot more interest if there truly were actual horror monsters werewolves alongside the spirit warrior ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, do they need servants or don't they? Anyway, main uses I had in mind was either a combat support unit, so they aren't so outnumbered. Or a way to easily get specialists/influence agents among humans who are now tied to them. <br /> <br /> Eh, as of W20 we have detailed breakdown for playing BSDs. I read it and there is really nothing human's haven't done. <br /> <br /> War wolves are a bit too specialized. But they are actually close, if too strictly Wyrm. <br /> <br /> Imagine werewolfs that can spread as fast as vampires. They would drown Garou under a tide of infectious furry manace. XD They do serve well enough to basically terrorize the vampires, elders included, in VTM tho, locking them inside cities and making hunting expeditions inside for delicious Vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T07:56:12-07:00","id":1533610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533608#post1533608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, do they need servants or don't they? Anyway, main uses I had in mind was either a combat support unit, so they aren't so outnumbered. Or a way to easily get specialists/influence agents among humans who are now tied to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your basic garou has 5+ strength, at LEAST 4 in stamina and regeneration in crinos, I think they'll be fine outnumbered. Besides, from my experience, garou often outnumber what they are trying to fight. And those fights give GAROU trouble, the combat support would be plain useless.<br /> <br /> And garou have specialist and agents helping them, their family members aka the kinfolk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533608#post1533608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, as of W20 we have detailed breakdown for playing BSDs. I read it and there is really nothing human's haven't done.</div> </div> </div> </div>What BSDs do, other garou don't do. BSD culture is VERY different from Gaian garou culture in significant ways. This isn't about content rating, this is about things like allies, breeding, religious views and strategies. When you play a BSD game, it is very different from a Gaian garou game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T08:08:47-07:00","id":1533613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533610#post1533610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What BSDs do, other garou don't do. BSD culture is VERY different from Gaian garou culture in significant ways. This isn't about content rating, this is about things like allies, breeding, religious views and strategies. When you play a BSD game, it is very different from a Gaian garou game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure BSD have different culture. Is that what you mean? <br /> With that argument, isn't playing Glass Walker also very different from playing Red Talon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T08:18:51-07:00","id":1533614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533613#post1533613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure BSD have different culture. Is that what you mean?<br /> With that argument, isn't playing Glass Walker also very different from playing Red Talon?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not at all similar. Glass Walkers and Red Talons obey the same set of laws, they follows the same cultural traditions even if they take different forms depending on the tribe, their sept culture follows the same rules, they gain renown from the same three categories, etc.<br /> <br /> BSDs have a different set of laws, different set of renown categories, different structure to their septs, they react differently to other supernaturals than Gaian garou.<br /> <br /> Gaian garou do not breed garou born intentionally, BSDs do. Gaian garou consider rape to be one of the worst wyrmy crimes, BSDs freely rape each other and their victims. BSDs have no limits to what they do other than rank, dominance and the veil. Gaian garou have VERY strict laws what they can do and can't do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T09:45:57-07:00","id":1533616,"title":"","content":"There are tales of very early versions of Werewolf doing the curse/infection thing; they typically collapsed into uneventful chronicles of acting normally interspersed by chaining yourself up at night. That quickly prompted the change over to what we have now, and left all of the matters of curses or plagues in Vampire territory. Divine punishment isn't even on the table; the setting has, thus far, only ever punished Garou via the terrible consequences of their pride-driven actions.<br /> <br /> Given the themes of W:tA, more numerous hordes of &quot;lesser&quot; servants would be completely out of place. There are rare and miraculous blessed beings referred to as Kami that the Garou will often engage in extreme violence and vigilance to protect as signs that Gaia yet lives and blesses the realm. Kami often tend to be a bit more fragile if they're living beings, and even Animate Lands have their limits, but not having battle-hardened Kami just leans further into the overall theme. As far as &quot;possessed&quot; beings go, these stand in stark contrast to fomori, who are typically used as cannon fodder by Wyrm factions left, right, and center, with the BSDs being no exception, even if they also breed another kind of intended cannon fodder among their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T11:19:56-07:00","id":1533623,"title":"","content":"I do feel being able to transmit lycanthropy like a virus or as a curse doesn\u2019t really mesh with the nature of the Garou, as described in Werewolf the Apocalypse - which is, as others have noted, Legendary Heroes who only look like Horror<br /> Movie Monsters (They can still be horrifying, but that\u2019s more the result of their own human/superhuman failings and the crushing burden of the Apocalypse War).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T13:32:14-07:00","id":1533638,"title":"","content":"In my own chronicles, I often have Garou bite Lost Cubs, Lunatics, and kinfolk who are suspected to be Garou, but who have not been able to change. The trauma of the bite often (but not always) is successful trigger that jumpstarts the First Change. The adrenalin of being stalked/hunted and the pain of the wound works well to push late changers into their First Change. It's my way of including that horror movie trope in a setting that otherwise doesn't allow it. <br /> <br /> I make a lot of minor setting changes like that in order to accommodate a lot of folklore, literary, and cinematic werewolf tropes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T23:27:21-07:00","id":1533682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls#post1533593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Well minds eye theater: werewolf the apocalypse along with the fan spinoff Werewolf the essentials has introduce the concept of the Bitten which is a human (and maybe kin folk) who was bit by a garou and is turned into a garou via magic. The only reason why most garou don't create bitten more often is because the creation process of a bitten messes up the spiritual environment. The BSD of course doesn't give a shit about the consequences and runs around and creating lost cubs. <br /> <br /> The main Tenets of two tribal alliances from Werewolf the essentials touch on the bitten<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tenets of the Dawn Tribes<br /> \u25cf Listen to your elders, build communities, and guide the young.<br /> \u25cf Detangling the Wyrm from the Weaver\u2019s corrupting web is key to restoring balance.<br /> \u25cf We Killi (WT:E term for full blooded garou ) are all cousins; the <b>Bitten </b>and the Warborn (WT:E term for metis) are our siblings in spirit. All are needed in the coming fight.<br /> \u25cf The old spirits have seen history repeat. We must revive their old ways to fight the Wyrm.<br /> \u25cf We serve neither king, wyrmcomer, nor colonist.<br /> \u25cf The moon reflects a bright sun, and we will share its light. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tenets of the Eastern Concordat<br /> \u25cf Strength comes from unity of purpose.<br /> \u25cf Balancing the world brings balance to the Triat. Balance within the Triat allows Gaia to survive.<br /> \u25cf Leadership belongs to those with ability, not lineage.<br /> \u25cf The <b>Bitten </b>and Hearthbound (a sort of kinfolk activists organization ) are allies by choice, never by force or coercion.<br /> \u25cf All of Gaia\u2019s children must come together now if there is to be any hope of a future. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T12:57:24-07:00","id":1533761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533682#post1533682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well minds eye theater: werewolf the apocalypse along with the fan spinoff Werewolf the essentials has introduce the concept of the Bitten which is a human (and maybe kin folk) who was bit by a garou and is turned into a garou via magic. The only reason why most garou don't create bitten more often is because the creation process of a bitten messes up the spiritual environment. The BSD of course doesn't give a shit about the consequences and runs around and creating lost cubs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the BSDs were written doing things that the writers should have thought about before going ham on them and pushing them through no matter what.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main Tenets of two tribal alliances from Werewolf the essentials touch on the bitten </div> </div> </div>Killi is actually a term that Bastet use for non-Bastet. It didn't get reprinted into W20, but it's in the Revised Player's Guide to the Changing Breeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T17:31:21-07:00","id":1533774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533761#post1533761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like the BSDs were written doing things that the writers should have thought about before going ham on them and pushing them through no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that and creating bitten seems to prevent the first change so BSD is denying future combatants while swelling they own ranks or creating headaches for the Gaian garou to deal with...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Killi is actually a term that Bastet use for non-Bastet. It didn't get reprinted into W20, but it's in the Revised Player's Guide to the Changing Breeds. </div> </div> </div>Well there's a high possibilities it's a Bastet loan word since the Dawn Tribes is explicitly a muti species alliance of fera. Kind of like north American version of the beast courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 04-07-2024, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T17:40:00-07:00","id":1533776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533774#post1533774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that and creating bitten seems to prevent the first change so BSD is denying future combatants while swelling they own ranks or creating headaches for the Gaian garou to deal with...</div> </div> </div> </div>If they can bite humans that way, there was never going to be a First Change. Also, there's nothing preventing a bitten werewolf from rebelling from the repellent and abusive BSDs if they push things too far too quickly. This has all the signatures of a kind of epidemic, and if it isn't addressed as the kind of potentially catastrophic swelling of super-powered werewolves it is, some vital piece of writing addressing the ramifications was left out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well there's a high possibilities it's a Bastet loan word since the Dawn Tribes is explicitly a muti species alliance of fera. Kind of like north American version of the beat courts. </div> </div> </div>Unlikely; those words tend to be very breed-specific when the authors aren't forgetting who uses them and making Shadow Lords refer to Bete (only done once!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T11:04:34-07:00","id":1534450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533614#post1533614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is not at all similar. Glass Walkers and Red Talons obey the same set of laws, they follows the same cultural traditions even if they take different forms depending on the tribe, their sept culture follows the same rules, they gain renown from the same three categories, etc.<br /> <br /> BSDs have a different set of laws, different set of renown categories, different structure to their septs, they react differently to other supernaturals than Gaian garou.<br /> <br /> Gaian garou do not breed garou born intentionally, BSDs do. Gaian garou consider rape to be one of the worst wyrmy crimes, BSDs freely rape each other and their victims. BSDs have no limits to what they do other than rank, dominance and the veil. Gaian garou have VERY strict laws what they can do and can't do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So you are convinced that notoriously cannibalistic forest savages and transhumanist technomancers are similar. Okay.<br /> <br /> Let's take a look at both litanies.<br /> <br /> <u>BSD LITANY</u><br /> <b>These 2 are unique to BSD</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Indulge Your Desires This is Your World</li> <li>All that is not Forbidden is Permitted</li> </ol><b>These 2 are religious tenets</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Serve the Wyrm\u2019s Will This is His Age</li> <li>The Spiral Awaits Those with Open Eyes</li> </ol><b>Perfectly the same as Gaian Garou. </b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Beware the Territory of Another</li> <li>Respect the Strength of the Mighty</li> <li>The First Share of the Kill for the Greatest in Station</li> <li>The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted</li> <li>Suffer Not Thy People to Tend Thy Sickness</li> <li>The Leader May Be Challenged at Any Time During Peace</li> <li>The Leader May Not Be Challenged During War</li> <li>Take No Action That Violates the Security of a Pit\u200b</li> </ol><br /> <u>GAIAN LITANY</u><br /> <b>These are unique to Gaian garou</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>\u200bGarou Shall Not Mate With Garou</li> <li>Ye Shall Not Eat the Flesh of Humans</li> <li>Accept an Honorable Surrender\u200b</li> <li>Respect Those Beneath Ye \u2014 All Are of Gaia</li> </ol>\u200b<b>\u200b\u200bThis is Religious</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Combat the Wyrm Wherever It Dwells and Whenever It Breeds</li> </ol><b>Perfectly the same as Gaian Garou.</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Respect the Territory of Another</li> <li>Submission to Those of Higher Station</li> <li>The First Share of the Kill for the Greatest in Station\u200b</li> <li>The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted\u200b</li> <li>Do Not Suffer Thy People to Tend Thy Sickness</li> <li>The Leader May Be Challenged at Any Time During Peace</li> <li>The Leader May Not Be Challenged During Wartime</li> <li>Ye Shall Take No Action That Causes a Caern to Be Violated</li> </ol>it is easy to see both litanies are mostly the same. even more so if you discount the purely religious tenets.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> and please enough with obsession over sex stuff. that was never asked about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 04-19-2024, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T15:59:57-07:00","id":1534464,"title":"","content":"I'm loving the talk involving WtE, though I need to make some clarifications. I'm writing them here because it's on topic.<br /> <br /> To be more specific, The Bite in WtE only works on unborn and kinfolk, and even then a person is just as likely to die from it as they are to change. This has made The Bite a modern topic of controversy among Garou. The Advent of The Bite comes from before the Dark Ages, and saw a resurgence in the Age of Apocalypse (nowish). Getting a bit ahead of myself. Let's talk about unborn!<br /> <br /> For the first time in the history of the Garou, the homids are facing a same date their Lupus cousins have been despairing over. Their population is dwindling. This is a truncated summarization, but effectively the Garou lost almost an entire generation of Cliath, and didn't realize what was happening until the damage had already been done. In short, the Wyrm's bastards suppressed the wolf spiritually within Garou. Over many years fewer and fewer potential Garou were experiencing the First Change, while older Garou kept getting older. <br /> <br /> Over time, the Garou have been noticing a steady increase in Lost cubs coming out of the woodwork, all of them describing a similar experience: They were bitten by some kind of animal, often described as wolf-like. They then undergo what can be described as the worst fever of their life, spanning an entire month. In this time they grow increasingly aggressive and irritable until finally they snap and shift into crisis, immediately frenzying. Unlike your typical First Change, without supernatural intervention the frenzy will last about 24 hours. Lastly, where all other Garou thankfully black out, the bitten are lucid, cognizant, and remember every last excruciating detail of their frenzy. The entire transformation experience leaves the bitten permanently marked. They are rendered sterile by the fever, and gain the Mark of the Predator flaw.<br /> <br /> Their supernatural nature is extremely hard to hide and others find it unsettling. The Unborn will subconsciously seek out Wyld spaces, and are magnetically drawn to the supernatural. The Black Spiral Dancers have greatly benefitted from this, recruiting more BSDs at a rate never seen before when newly Bitten come right to them.<br /> <br /> When the tide of Lost Cubs didn't seem to be turn, initially elders of tribes feigned ignorance, denying their involvement in these bites, but eventually they admitted that indeed The Bite was being employed by tribes. When facing the reality of impending extinction brought on by the Wyrm suppressing a generation, and acknowledging the Black Spiral Dancers had already begun using it, the other tribes were forced to adopt it in kind to prevent more of their own from falling to the Wyrm; a tragic arms race. <br /> <br /> The outlook on Bitten is often one handled on a Sept to Sept basis, and often mirrors that Sept's treatment of crinos-born' Garou. Several Garou strongly dislike the bite. It's a major risk of a kinfolk dying while undergoing the process, and many are demanding a better way to address Unborn. With the BSDs happily churning out more Garou than ever before, for the time being, it's become necessary.<br /> <br /> There are benefits to this of course. The Stolen Moons are seeing their numbers plateau. Where a Kinfolk no longer needs to undergo the rite of sacred rebirth, the bite is a much more attractive option. It also lets Kinfolk get more directly involved in the war against the Wyrm. Crinos-born are enormous fans of the bite, because it means that at long last, they have a vector for creating new Garou that wouldn't have existed before. <br /> <br /> Is the bite good in the long run? That's for Players and Storytellers to decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T16:23:50-07:00","id":1534466,"title":"","content":"It still seems like someone forgot about the Birthing Plague of the Ratkin and decided to just go for broke on Universal Monsters tropes because they were playing to the gallery on V:tM and didn't see why it wouldn't work with W:tA. (Spoilers: Pretty much nothing that's good for V:tM is good for W:tA)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T17:57:38-07:00","id":1534471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1534464#post1534464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm loving the talk involving WtE, though I need to make some clarifications. I'm writing them here because it's on topic.<br /> <br /> To be more specific, The Bite in WtE only works on unborn and kinfolk, and even then a person is just as likely to die from it as they are to change. This has made The Bite a modern topic of controversy among Garou. The Advent of The Bite comes from before the Dark Ages, and saw a resurgence in the Age of Apocalypse (nowish). Getting a bit ahead of myself. Let's talk about unborn!<br /> <br /> For the first time in the history of the Garou, the homids are facing a same date their Lupus cousins have been despairing over. Their population is dwindling. This is a truncated summarization, but effectively the Garou lost almost an entire generation of Cliath, and didn't realize what was happening until the damage had already been done. In short, the Wyrm's bastards suppressed the wolf spiritually within Garou. Over many years fewer and fewer potential Garou were experiencing the First Change, while older Garou kept getting older.<br /> <br /> Over time, the Garou have been noticing a steady increase in Lost cubs coming out of the woodwork, all of them describing a similar experience: They were bitten by some kind of animal, often described as wolf-like. They then undergo what can be described as the worst fever of their life, spanning an entire month. In this time they grow increasingly aggressive and irritable until finally they snap and shift into crisis, immediately frenzying. Unlike your typical First Change, without supernatural intervention the frenzy will last about 24 hours. Lastly, where all other Garou thankfully black out, the bitten are lucid, cognizant, and remember every last excruciating detail of their frenzy. The entire transformation experience leaves the bitten permanently marked. They are rendered sterile by the fever, and gain the Mark of the Predator flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this method of creating by bite would only give the BSD's an advantage in the long run, while the rest of the tribes wouldn't choose just anyone, they have relatives, but anyone from outside would have to be evaluated, I at least believe they wouldn't have very high criteria for choosing new Garou, whereas the BSD wouldn't mind creating newbies to become disposable soldiers or making them mistreated servants, so there's this problem of quantity. An interesting point would be that the lupines would probably increase their numbers a lot and perhaps even surpass the homids, I even imagine a Red Talon asking if they still need the homids.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1534464#post1534464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Crinos-born are enormous fans of the bite, because it means that at long last, they have a vector for creating new Garou that wouldn't have existed before.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this part of the Crinos, wouldn't it be possible for them to feel threatened? In the past, Crinos were killed at birth, but they became tolerated due to the low number of Garou births, but now that they can create more in a shorter period of time, what is their position?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1534464#post1534464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the bite good in the long run? That's for Players and Storytellers to decide.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good question.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T22:39:10-07:00","id":1534478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1534471#post1534471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this part of the Crinos, wouldn't it be possible for them to feel threatened? In the past, Crinos were killed at birth, but they became tolerated due to the low number of Garou births, but now that they can create more in a shorter period of time, what is their position?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, yeah. A Bitten and a Crinos-born fill the same slot, and a Bitten comes with WAYY less burdens for the sept. The Bitten can somewhat go into public without breaking the Veil, while Crinos-born in WtE still have fantasy traits. A Bitten doesn't take a warrior out of commission, a Crinos-born does if not kill the garou who carried them. A Bitten doesn't need to be raised in solely the sept for 10 years to get anything out of them.<br /> <br /> While some Crinos-born might see the Bite as a way to procreate, others might feel the Bite will mean no future Crinos-born child is kept alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T03:07:36-07:00","id":1534483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1534450#post1534450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So you are convinced that notoriously cannibalistic forest savages and transhumanist technomancers are similar. Okay.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>They have more in common with each other than with the BSDs, they follow the same Litany and are members of the same Nation. You can have a Walker and a Talon in the same pack. You can't have a BSD and a Walker in the same pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1534450#post1534450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's take a look at both litanies.<br /> <br /> <u>BSD LITANY</u><br /> <b>These 2 are unique to BSD</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Indulge Your Desires This is Your World</li> <li>All that is not Forbidden is Permitted</li> </ol><b>These 2 are religious tenets</b>[LIST=1][*]Serve the Wyrm\u2019s Will This is His Age[*]The Spiral Awaits Those with Open Eyes<br /> <br /> <u>GAIAN LITANY</u><br /> <b>These are unique to Gaian garou</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>\u200bGarou Shall Not Mate With Garou</li> <li>Ye Shall Not Eat the Flesh of Humans</li> <li>Accept an Honorable Surrender\u200b</li> <li>Respect Those Beneath Ye \u2014 All Are of Gaia</li> </ol>\u200b<b>\u200b\u200bThis is Religious</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Combat the Wyrm Wherever It Dwells and Whenever It Breeds</li> </ol><br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Erhm, I suggest you look at these tenets that differ from one another, because they send a WHOLE different message.<br /> <br /> Because BSDs Litany says;<br /> Kill, rape, torture, breed with other garou, eat humans,convert as many as you want to the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Gaian Litany says;<br /> Do not breed with other garou, don't kill others during challenge, do respect things that are not garou, fight the force of corruption that makes people miserable.<br /> <br /> I don't know how to explain to you that there is a difference between those two.<br /> <br /> The rest of the tenets they have in common? Stuff related to running a werewolf society.<br /> <br /> Also, the sex stuff is part of BSDs, as they want to outbreed the Gaians. That is a difference between Gaians and them as Gaians do not do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 04-20-2024, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T06:29:46-07:00","id":1534488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1534450#post1534450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> notoriously cannibalistic forest savages</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really a good description of Red Talons because it makes them sound like they were in any way ever human, and anthropophagy tends to be one of those &quot;depending on the author&quot; things, with many an author having written that as &quot;not really, maybe a camp that's not in the majority&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> transhumanist technomancers </div> </div> </div>That describes exactly one camp, which, ah, isn't really doing so great on numbers since most of them were punished for their &quot;let's test fetish implants out on lupus Garou and see if it works!&quot; stunt backfired horribly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T07:03:35-07:00","id":1534489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1534464#post1534464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the first time in the history of the Garou, the homids are facing a same date their Lupus cousins have been despairing over. Their population is dwindling. This is a truncated summarization, but effectively the Garou lost almost an entire generation of Cliath, and didn't realize what was happening until the damage had already been done. In short, the Wyrm's bastards suppressed the wolf spiritually within Garou. Over many years fewer and fewer potential Garou were experiencing the First Change, while older Garou kept getting older.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are new homids being born normally now, or are the Garou still reliant on the Bite (or lupus, I suppose, since you speak of this as being a homid problem) to make more of themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T18:10:08-07:00","id":1534514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1534450#post1534450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So you are convinced that notoriously cannibalistic forest savages and transhumanist technomancers are similar. Okay.<br /> <br /> Let's take a look at both litanies.<br /> <br /> <u>BSD LITANY</u><br /> <b>These 2 are unique to BSD</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Indulge Your Desires This is Your World</li> <li>All that is not Forbidden is Permitted</li> </ol><b>These 2 are religious tenets</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Serve the Wyrm\u2019s Will This is His Age</li> <li>The Spiral Awaits Those with Open Eyes</li> </ol><b>Perfectly the same as Gaian Garou. </b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Beware the Territory of Another</li> <li>Respect the Strength of the Mighty</li> <li>The First Share of the Kill for the Greatest in Station</li> <li>The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted</li> <li>Suffer Not Thy People to Tend Thy Sickness</li> <li>The Leader May Be Challenged at Any Time During Peace</li> <li>The Leader May Not Be Challenged During War</li> <li>Take No Action That Violates the Security of a Pit</li> </ol><br /> <u>GAIAN LITANY</u><br /> <b>These are unique to Gaian garou</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>\u200bGarou Shall Not Mate With Garou</li> <li>Ye Shall Not Eat the Flesh of Humans</li> <li>Accept an Honorable Surrender\u200b</li> <li>Respect Those Beneath Ye \u2014 All Are of Gaia</li> </ol>\u200b<b>\u200b\u200bThis is Religious</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Combat the Wyrm Wherever It Dwells and Whenever It Breeds</li> </ol><b>Perfectly the same as Gaian Garou.</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Respect the Territory of Another</li> <li>Submission to Those of Higher Station</li> <li>The First Share of the Kill for the Greatest in Station\u200b</li> <li>The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted\u200b</li> <li>Do Not Suffer Thy People to Tend Thy Sickness</li> <li>The Leader May Be Challenged at Any Time During Peace</li> <li>The Leader May Not Be Challenged During Wartime</li> <li>Ye Shall Take No Action That Causes a Caern to Be Violated</li> </ol>it is easy to see both litanies are mostly the same. even more so if you discount the purely religious tenets.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> and please enough with obsession over sex stuff. that was never asked about.</div> </div> </div> </div>And your take away is that these are somehow similar?<br /> <br /> Litany is by its design and intent religious in its significance. The Garou Litany is about reaffirming social norms and the obligation of the Garou to actually facilitate a hiearachy meant for war channeling the destructive tendancies of the Garou while making them concious of their position as protectors and aware that their power does not give them carte-blanche to be utter monsters. A Red Talon and Glass Walker might be philosophically opposed, but they will fight side by side.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Black Spiral Dancer Litany is all about power, corruption and doing what ever you will in the service of the wyrm. It's not about a stable society, it's about making sure you channel your monstrosity creatively. Just reading the writeups should be enough to illustrate that just because there is overlarp doesn't mean all that much in identifying how the BSD's operate.<br /> <br /> <br /> And its hard not to talk about the sex stuff considering that:<br /> <br /> <b>Indulge Your Desires - This is Your World<br /> All that is not Forbidden is Permitted\u200b</b><br /> <br /> Are core to their treatment of kinfolk and their captives and how and why they seek to mass create new BSD's while spreading the misery of the Wyrm to all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T11:19:17-07:00","id":1562230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1533774#post1533774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that and creating bitten seems to prevent the first change</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you become a werewolf without undergoing a first change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"htt