ou survive the month long sickness that come along it and don't get consumed by rage and degrade into a feral monster. Then Congratulations Youre a garou. Granted one that's has some stigma attached due to they're sterile, the elders not how it works beyond spirit shenanigans and most of the other bitten are basically BSD shovel heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T05:32:47-07:00","id":1562255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1562253#post1562253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well to be fair you could find another garou to bite you then you might get turned into a wolf. Assuming you survive the month long sickness that come along it and don't get consumed by rage and degrade into a feral monster. Then Congratulations Youre a garou. Granted one that's has some stigma attached due to they're sterile, the elders not how it works beyond spirit shenanigans and most of the other bitten are basically BSD shovel heads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, heaping helpings of pseudo-V:tM slop!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T07:24:48-07:00","id":1562259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1562253#post1562253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted one that's has some stigma attached due to they're sterile,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Garou are forbidden to mate with other Garou anyways, so that's not really something I'm concerned about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T11:57:58-07:00","id":1562315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1562259#post1562259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Garou are forbidden to mate with other Garou anyways, so that's not really something I'm concerned about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but theoretically with the Bitten, there would be little to no evidence that anything of the sort happened unless you caught them in flagrante delicto or soon after (the wolf nose knows).<br /> <br /> Also, as a question to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25848\" data-vbnamecard=\"25848\">MrornX</a> were there any indications that they had intended to extend the Bitten concept to Fera?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T12:50:47-07:00","id":1562320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1562315#post1562315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, as a question to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25848\" data-vbnamecard=\"25848\">MrornX</a> were there any indications that they had intended to extend the Bitten concept to Fera?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well most fera can't do it as far but there's some instances of mammalian fera turning people into the bitten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T16:58:11-07:00","id":1563385,"title":"","content":"A source cite tidbit for the conversation, particularly Re: some of the questions about The Bite, as per the MET BNS edition it comes from, regarding Fera and Black Spiral Dancers. <br /> tl;dr<br /> - Fera can create Bitten<br /> - Black Spiral Dancers (or other Fallen who no longer have a connection to Gaia) cannot create Bitten<br /> <br /> Mind's Eye Theatre Werewolf the Apocalypse (&quot;Fera and the Bitten&quot; sidebar, page 368):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although initially the Bite seemed reserved only for Garou, this new plague has spread to all of the Fera breeds, allowing them to inflict the Bite on their Unborn. Some shapeshifters take this fact as proof that the Bite is an engineered plague deliberately released into the Garou Nation. The Ratkin privately claim that the emergence of the Bite is a sign that they shall rise to rule the world in a new era they\u2019ve deemed the Age of the Rat. Strangely, Black Spiral Dancers and Skin Dancers have not yet been able to enact the Bite on Unborn, suggesting that this new plague requires some sort of Gaian spiritual connection. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T22:23:43-07:00","id":1563396,"title":"","content":"Actually, if we're talking about 'discount werewolves' created through biting, I like to imagine them as something along the lines of Balverines (from the Fable franchise), or the earliest generations of Lycans from the Underworld series.<br /> <br /> To summarize it, these were werewolves / werewolf-like creatures who became permanently stuck in their monster state and couldn't return back to human form.<br /> <br /> Well, except for in Fable 3, where that seemed to have been retconned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 08-24-2026, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T01:37:30-07:00","id":1563526,"title":"","content":"I want to circle back to the initial pitch here, but with a notable change: a Bite that turns a rando into a Gaian &quot;wolf Fomori&quot;...but it's not something done by Garou. Instead, it happens through the vector of a Gaian <i>spirit</i>. Probably a wolf spirit, obviously.<br /> <br /> Imagine for a moment. It's the Age of Apocalypse. The world is dying. The Wyrm and its minions are gaining ground. The Garou aren't powerful enough to stem the tide themselves, and other shifters aren't helping matters.<br /> <br /> Gaia decides to start throwing things against the wall, in the hopes SOMETHING sticks and pushes matters in the favor of her own survival. One of these are the Kami, of course. One of these might be some kind of hypothetical &quot;Dog-Garou&quot;, why not. (That's for another thread).<br /> <br /> But another is &quot;just make Diet Garou&quot;. What's more, it seems unusually effective (those Cairn-stealing Mages might say some BS about &quot;Mythic Threads&quot; or something). So, whenever the veil between Umbra and mortal world waxes thin, a wolf spirit stalks the wilderness on the full moon. Prowling, seeking, hunting. Not to feed, but to BITE.<br /> <br /> Maybe it requires the subject to be Kinfolk. Maybe it doesn't, and it's purely a matter of whoever the spirit finds. Whatever the case, it bites campers and hunters and whoever else. They get sick, with their symptoms waning and waxing with the moon. Some die outright, the stress of their body trying and failing to bond with a mote of Gaian spirit proving too much. Perhaps they fight off the &quot;infection&quot; entirely. But some see it settle into their blood. When the full moon rises again, they change.<br /> <br /> I definitely wouldn't give them the full Garou package. That's not what they're here to do, and if Gaia could just MAKE more Garou it wouldn't be in such dire straights. But they're got some strengths of wolf shifters, and some weaknesses too. Maybe the capacity to learn simple Gifts, if a spirit is willing to teach? (I'm not terribly inclined towards this option, since we're straying too far from the &quot;Hollywood Werewolf&quot; angle). Maybe they can pass their &quot;infection&quot; on to others? (I'd only have that work during the full moon, to prevent a runaway pandemic). And, unless the &quot;Wolf Fomor&quot; is particularly strong willed, they're not wholly in control of themselves during their &quot;episodes&quot;.<br /> <br /> It might be a neat plot hook or potential antagonist/ally source. It certainly dodges the problem of &quot;PCs factory farm Bite victims&quot; or matters of setting-warping imbalance, because no Garou have control over when or to whom it happens. Rather, it's every Garou (Gaian or BSD) having to REACT to a situation outside their control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T12:03:28-07:00","id":1563542,"title":"","content":"I think that's a more interesting angle, though I wouldn't ascribe deliberate action to Gaia in this sense. But that's neither here or there.<br /> <br /> The real cause would be unknowable, the point is that those Kami exist and are spreading.<br /> <br /> No need for consistency, either. Just like fomor, they may be harder to predict and varied in the end result. Instead of a defined template, it's a chart of options and any given individual has a random selection of them.<br /> <br /> Some control the transformation, some have a Gift or more, some have access to the Umbra, some are conscious during Change, some are empowered to perform Rites, whatever you think some of them do. And most don't.<br /> <br /> Another interesting option is that this may be a way to put some Garou expectations in check. Some may be more spiritually blessed than the Garou themselves, and the telltale signs are not what Garou culture would point to. Maybe some have traits traditionally associated with the Wyrm, but in this individual they serve Gaia or at least don't reek of Wyrm Taint.<br /> <br /> Other splats can also get versions like that. Not a regular member, but Kami that imitate them while following distinct, inscrutable rules. The Kami versions are ecologically sound, though. Not simply mutant aberrations, but something that can carve a proper niche in the system. Or maybe reveal a niche that existed all along if a splat follow their true nature (according to this scenario, not necessarily to their gameline).<br /> <br /> Kami vampires, Shapechangers, Mages, Fae, Ghosts, Mummies, Imbued and Demons. How could they imitate yet differ from the originals? How could they twist the concept, or bring old folklore concepts, in order to work as adapted species with a proper niche? What would they look like in a version that isn't just completely compatible with Werewolf perspective, but also definitely Gaian? And all that while being recent and unheard of before, or would it be better if such things existed in the past and this is just a resurgence?<br /> <br /> But the wolves alone would already throw a lot in the cogs of how the Nation views the world and their own place in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T14:57:30-07:00","id":1563547,"title":"","content":"Ratkin could probably find a way to forcefully activate the changing seed through viral pathogens, if we haven't already.<br /> <br /> But the stupid, smelly, Garou Nation would need to learn how to sit and beg, before we agreed to share it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T17:17:43-07:00","id":1564578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533593-infectious-werewolf-bites-werewolf-version-of-ghouls?p=1534489#post1534489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are new homids being born normally now, or are the Garou still reliant on the Bite (or lupus, I suppose, since you speak of this as being a homid problem) to make more of themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the late reply. <br /> <br /> There are, yes, though at a rate lower than before. To be clear though, there are both Unborn lupus as well as homids. In general, less Gaians are experiencing their first change, even with the advent of the Bitten. From a first-person perspective, to play a Gaian that experienced their First Change in the Age of Heroes is something that is going to turn heads and get all kinds of Gaians coming out of the woodwork, for better and for worse. To put it in perspective, a young Gaian will find many Septs at the start of their game to be a bit of a bridge club (that is, them being the youngest person in the room) until they meet their other respective packmates. Feuds will be a little older, a little more entrenched, grief considered long-settled will resurface, and a common thread of &quot;what can we do differently this time&quot; will be at the back of many minds of elders and mentors. For some, the Apocalypse came for them and even if they survived, their principals died, and the existence of a new cub, whether born or bitten, is a living foil to that notion. To others, they maybe had less elders mentoring them for a dearth of living heroes in their locale, and with the moon bridge network collapsed, even getting to these lost cubs could be days to weeks depending on one's locale, making an immediate, broad social consensus a lot less absolute.<br /> <br /> Even as of 2nd edition it was encouraged to confront the old, stuck ways of some tribe members, and here its a little more in the forefront without being the shotgun blast of &quot;none of the elders know anything and all traditions are bad&quot; that w5 offers. The hurt is more measurable, and the demographical breakdowns make the need for leadership to listen more to its future leaders more practical. The sins of the past are more immediate. In short, being a new pup is a bit of a marvel here. The frequency and density of these demographics will vary between one sept and another, depending on how the local Gaians have responded to the many outcomes of the Age of Apocalypse. Some Septs are &quot;business as usual&quot; and hardly recognize them. Others may be in regions that are saturated with it and it is a central concern. In this Age, the makeup of your Sept matters a lot in what its political outlook ultimately holds. There was a period in which no Gaians were experiencing their First Change. Once the Storm Eater was bound to its prison realm once more, things began to improve, but that was still just a couple years ago in this setting, and the players are coming into a battlefield with corpses that aren't done decomposing yet and grass not yet overgrowing what were once trenches, figuratively speaking. What would this look like at your own table?<br /> <br /> I guess to answer the question, its less a 'it is this state and is always to be this state' so much as a moment of political flux, whose destination is ultimately in the hands of the narrative the ST is telling. It could mean a lot, or it could mean little. That's what this is...a colorful option in a broader narrative palette.<br /> <br /> As for the reliance on the Bite...not all are Bitten, and many kinfolk do not undergo the bite. If one is playing a Bitten they, presumably, would be one who survived such an ordeal. The biggest meta reasons I have seen for players preferring bitten largely center around a few key points:<ul><li>They want to play a newly changed garou but don't wish to play a child or a teenager.</li> <li>They want to explore charach story themes without dealing with childbirth</li> <li>They want to experience common werewolf movie tropes, such as a month-long transformation theme that is terrifying both to the werewolf and their victim(s)</li> <li>They want to explore trauma as a storytelling vehicle (the fact they remember every moment of their change, and the change lasting a full twelve hours, offers that in spades).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}